# Parallel branches (cxado core)

Use **separate git branches** so multiple agents can work different phases concurrently. Phase rhythm: [core-workflow-chain.mdc](core-workflow-chain.mdc).

## Branch naming

Use the prefix defined in project overlay (e.g. `cys-agi/phase-<NN>-<slug>`, `engage/phase-<NN>-<slug>`).

- `<NN>` = phase number from master plan.
- `<slug>` = short kebab-case from phase title.

## Starting a phase

From up-to-date `main`, create the branch and record it in the status table. Push and open a PR; **do not merge** unless critic APPROVE or the user explicitly asked.

## Concurrency

- Independent phases: separate branches OK.
- Serial dependencies: wait for merge, then `git rebase origin/main`.
- **One branch = one phase.**

## Merge discipline

| Rule | Action |
|------|--------|
| Merge soon | After critic APPROVE, merge within the same work wave |
| One source of truth | New work from `git pull origin main` |
| Before next parallel stream | Merge completed phases first |

After merge: run project verify commands from overlay, then notify open branches to rebase.

Git hygiene (secrets, `.gitignore`): [core-workflow-chain.mdc](core-workflow-chain.mdc).
